<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pandua, Malda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hazrat Pandua</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pandua is a historic town in the Malda district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, north of the old capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Gaur</a>. In the 14th century the Ilyas Shahi sultans made it the capital of the Bengal Sultanate, and its monuments include the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adina-mosque">Adina Mosque</a> and the Eklakhi Mausoleum. The court returned to Gaur in the 15th century, and Pandua declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pandua-malda.jpg" alt="Pandua, Malda" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amitabha Gupta · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adina_Mosque_at_Malda_district_of_West_Bengal_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
